#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059416 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69e91ce7-259a-5a11-bb79-7e6ad7ea86d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "4cd24c10-1838-5f4b-ac88-cfbfc2ec4c21" :question/math-academy-id "e-3518" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x - 30^{\\circ} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v) = \\sin u\\cos v - \\cos u\\sin v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and\n\n$$\nv=30^{\\circ}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (x - 30^{∘}) &= \\sin x\\cos 30^{∘} - \\cos x\\sin 30^{∘} \\\\\n&= \\sin x \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) - \\cos x \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x}{2} - \\frac{\\cos x}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x - \\cos x}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059417 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "7341638b-3c0f-5c10-8b7d-a2c313607bed" :question/math-academy-id "e-3519" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$ without using a calculator.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$.*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(x-y) = \\sin x\\cos y - \\cos x\\sin y\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\sin (\\frac{π}{3} - \\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{3})\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}) - \\cos (\\frac{π}{3})\\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{6} - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b12a7b7-1df3-5203-934e-8820604de3de" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/id #uuid "0ce71d86-7470-5d53-ac94-20b473889dee" :question/math-academy-id "e-9983" :question/problem "Express $\\sin\\left(x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$." :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v) = \\sin{u}\\cos{v} + \\cos{u}\\sin{v}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u = x$ and\n\n$$\nv = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (x + \\frac{π}{6}) &= \\sin x\\cos (\\frac{π}{6}) + \\cos x\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\sin x \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) + \\cos x \\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x}{2} + \\frac{\\cos x}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\sin x + \\cos x}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "213eda96-c41d-5361-9da9-8349617014f1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9db298b6-b43c-5118-821f-e87730da0fde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256136} {:answer/id #uuid "373b3acf-1032-5212-8772-30000e77f8a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256137} {:answer/id #uuid "617e3053-e2df-5bcf-9956-b1393c90b5ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256138} {:answer/id #uuid "c6074a87-c3cd-5b5b-a8c2-9e956d51355a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}-\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256139} {:answer/id #uuid "cb18d673-cab0-5c7f-9d69-582d7372ae9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb18d673-cab0-5c7f-9d69-582d7372ae9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256140} :answer-field/id #uuid "31ba84cd-7a5e-5d0f-bf78-55cc8ff4302b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cd2c2bca-9519-5215-8935-6519f49e527f" :question/math-academy-id "q-119007" :question/problem "What is the exact value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})?$" :question/worked-solution "The angle ${75}^{∘}$ is not a special angle. However, we can rewrite it as the sum of two special angles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{75}^{∘}={45}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $x={45}^{∘}$ and $y={30}^{∘},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({45}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}+\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "69e91ce7-259a-5a11-bb79-7e6ad7ea86d4" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying Expressions in Degrees Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efab77f2